1
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,540
<i>If I had to describe him...</i>

2
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:14,640
<i>He was like the sun.</i>

3
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:25,720
<i>His dazzling warmth and attitude</i>

4
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:30,260
<i>put a smile on everyone's faces.</i>

5
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:39,880
<i>I was sure our paths would never cross.</i>

6
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:50,900
<i>At least, that's what I'd assumed.</i>

7
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:07,610
Does that mean you like me, Suzuki?

8
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:14,780
Hey.

9
00:01:16,850 --> 00:01:19,570
Don't shy away.

10
00:01:19,570 --> 00:01:21,210
Give me an answer.

11
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:26,160
<i>How did I get here?</i>

12
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:32,690
<i>Am I dreaming?</i>

13
00:01:33,410 --> 00:01:35,490
<i>Or is this...</i>

14
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:44,140
[Episode 1]

15
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:47,090
[WIP]

16
00:01:47,090 --> 00:01:48,790
[6:30 AM - Alarm]

17
00:01:56,810 --> 00:01:58,490
Crap.

18
00:02:03,350 --> 00:02:06,640
<i>Hajime Suzuki, high school sophomore.</i>

19
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:10,660
<i>I like to write stories and daydream.</i>

20
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:14,880
[Stars in the Deep Sea]

21
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:19,540
<i>My genre of choice is BL.</i>

22
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:22,650
<i>In short, I'm a "fudanshi".</i>
[T/N: Guy who likes BL (Boys Love)]

23
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:29,480
<i>But I only enjoy consuming BL.</i>

24
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:33,590
<i>I haven't ever fallen for a real guy.</i>

25
00:02:39,230 --> 00:02:41,800
<i>If anything,</i>

26
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:45,630
<i>romance isn't really for a guy like me.</i>

27
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:53,660
<i>Girls treat me like thin air anyway.</i>

28
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:55,040
Hey, um...

29
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:56,830
- It's mine now.
- Gimme.

30
00:02:56,830 --> 00:02:59,250
What? No!

31
00:02:59,250 --> 00:03:01,050
- Can I...
- Nuh-uh.

32
00:03:01,050 --> 00:03:03,210
You're not having it.

33
00:03:03,210 --> 00:03:05,280
Never!

34
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:11,740
<i>Long story short,
I've given up on relationships.</i>

35
00:03:14,270 --> 00:03:15,820
Did you finish the assignment?

36
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:18,150
- Shoot, I forgot.
- Let's cram together.

37
00:03:18,150 --> 00:03:19,730
- What?
- Come on, please?

38
00:03:19,730 --> 00:03:23,090
- No thanks.
- I'm begging you.

39
00:03:23,090 --> 00:03:27,400
<i>I don't even have a friend.</i>

40
00:03:37,030 --> 00:03:39,550
<i>I'm a complete loner.</i>

41
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:46,750
<i>My renowned classmates on the other hand,</i>

42
00:03:46,750 --> 00:03:50,150
<i>are my complete opposite.</i>

43
00:03:51,090 --> 00:03:52,460
- Morning.
- Hey guys!

44
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:56,020
- Morning.
- 'Sup?

45
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:59,680
<i>Yuma Saeki.</i>

46
00:04:02,290 --> 00:04:05,830
<i>A good-looking, sociable fashionista.</i>

47
00:04:06,770 --> 00:04:08,960
[Yuma Saeki - 32,000 Followers]

48
00:04:11,130 --> 00:04:12,400
- Morning, Koha.
- Morning.

49
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:14,540
Your makeup looks different today.

50
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:16,870
Oh, yeah. Does it look weird?

51
00:04:16,870 --> 00:04:19,910
Nope. You look as cute as ever.

52
00:04:19,910 --> 00:04:20,940
Shut up!

53
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:24,290
All right, enough flirting you two.

54
00:04:24,290 --> 00:04:27,290
Our resident meathead is jealous.

55
00:04:27,290 --> 00:04:30,580
Hey, I'm no meathead.

56
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:31,950
I'm a "muscle"-head.

57
00:04:31,950 --> 00:04:33,540
- Same difference.
- Yeah.

58
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:37,200
As if. See? Muscles, not meat.

59
00:04:37,870 --> 00:04:40,130
<i>Shun Iwasaki.</i>

60
00:04:40,130 --> 00:04:42,320
<i>A member of our judo team.</i>

61
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:45,410
<i>Known for his strength and physique.</i>

62
00:04:45,410 --> 00:04:48,240
But he was at a disadvantage! That's crazy...

63
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:50,440
- Score!
- He's the best in the prefecture.

64
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:53,460
I bet he'll be recruited
for the national team.

65
00:04:54,910 --> 00:04:56,990
- Yeah, yeah.
- Iwasaki.

66
00:04:56,990 --> 00:04:59,610
Did you do the math worksheet due today?

67
00:04:59,610 --> 00:05:01,900
Shoot, I forgot.

68
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:03,530
Takeuchi.

69
00:05:03,530 --> 00:05:05,080
Let me copy yours.

70
00:05:05,080 --> 00:05:07,020
Not happening. Do it yourself.

71
00:05:07,020 --> 00:05:09,400
<i>Tomoaki Takeuchi.</i>

72
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:13,570
<i>A chill guy, known for his smarts.</i>

73
00:05:13,570 --> 00:05:17,050
Holy cow, he got straight A's!

74
00:05:17,050 --> 00:05:21,130
Takeuchi always scores top ten
on the national mock exams.

75
00:05:21,130 --> 00:05:23,920
How? I don't ever see him study.

76
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:26,600
He must be a genius.

77
00:05:28,230 --> 00:05:32,560
All right everyone, settle down.

78
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:34,590
Hey, where's Serizawa?

79
00:05:34,590 --> 00:05:36,650
Beats me.

80
00:05:36,650 --> 00:05:39,020
Probably late again.

81
00:05:39,020 --> 00:05:41,040
<i>And the last member of their posse...</i>

82
00:05:49,370 --> 00:05:53,150
What's up, class?

83
00:05:53,150 --> 00:05:54,790
<i>Haruto Serizawa.</i>

84
00:05:54,790 --> 00:05:57,210
Tone it down, Serizawa.

85
00:05:57,210 --> 00:05:59,150
You're not even on time.

86
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:00,730
I'm practically on time.

87
00:06:00,730 --> 00:06:03,030
Which means you're late.

88
00:06:03,030 --> 00:06:04,760
For real?

89
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:07,020
- Cut me some slack, Mr. Usami.
- Not happening.

90
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:10,870
Aw, pretty please?

91
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:13,330
You're not changing my mind, kid.

92
00:06:13,330 --> 00:06:14,610
Now get to your seat.

93
00:06:14,610 --> 00:06:16,780
Yes, sir.

94
00:06:20,150 --> 00:06:22,400
<i>These four good-looking dudes,</i>

95
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:26,630
<i>are the most popular guys in our school.</i>

96
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:54,660
Score!

97
00:06:54,660 --> 00:07:00,340
<i>When my sophomore year began,
I became classmates with Serizawa.</i>

98
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:03,330
<i>He quickly had me enthralled.</i>

99
00:07:05,170 --> 00:07:07,880
He's as cool as ever.

100
00:07:11,970 --> 00:07:15,770
<i>Because in my eyes,</i>

101
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:19,830
<i>Serizawa was the perfect top.</i>

102
00:07:19,830 --> 00:07:23,520
[Haruto Serizawa]

103
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:25,520
<i>And so,</i>

104
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:30,660
<i>I began writing a BL novel
with Serizawa as the main character.</i>

105
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:32,360
It's definitely over here.

106
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:35,810
You sure? You were wrong yesterday.

107
00:07:41,570 --> 00:07:46,650
<i>If anyone found out about my little hobby...</i>

108
00:07:54,710 --> 00:07:56,610
Let's get outta here.

109
00:07:56,610 --> 00:07:59,160
Yeah. Anyone up for karaoke?

110
00:08:00,570 --> 00:08:02,700
Where is it?

111
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:06,270
You looking for something, Suzuki?

112
00:08:08,530 --> 00:08:10,660
S-Seri...

113
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:12,970
Serizawa?

114
00:08:15,590 --> 00:08:17,610
Um, I...

115
00:08:18,820 --> 00:08:20,870
Let me guess.

116
00:08:21,910 --> 00:08:23,620
Looking for this?

117
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:27,650
Wh-Why... H-How...

118
00:08:27,650 --> 00:08:29,550
You were sitting where I found it,

119
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:32,640
so I assumed.

120
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:34,090
Here.

121
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:39,620
Makes sense.

122
00:08:41,790 --> 00:08:44,990
Th-Thank you.

123
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,670
Huh?

124
00:08:52,370 --> 00:08:56,600
You write about a "Haruto Serizawa" in here.

125
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,090
Is that supposed to be me?

126
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:13,480
<i>It's so over.</i>

127
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:18,520
Suzuki?

128
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:22,930
Hello? Anyone home?

129
00:09:24,050 --> 00:09:28,810
I... I...

130
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:30,830
I'm so sorry!

131
00:09:30,830 --> 00:09:33,850
Huh? Hey, your notebook!

132
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:29,560
<i>I ended up running away.</i>

133
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:34,080
What do I do? Serizawa's definitely mad.

134
00:10:36,110 --> 00:10:38,000
<i>Actually,</i>

135
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,990
<i>there's a bigger problem...</i>

136
00:10:41,990 --> 00:10:45,150
[Year 1, Class 3]

137
00:10:45,150 --> 00:10:48,690
Did you hear what Suzuki reads?

138
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:49,920
- Yeah.
- I can't believe it.

139
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:51,500
It sort of grosses me out.

140
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:52,600
Same.

141
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:54,310
Why would a guy like BL?

142
00:10:54,310 --> 00:10:56,850
- Beats me.
- Maybe he's eyeing you.

143
00:10:56,850 --> 00:10:58,740
- Dude, not funny.
- You sure?

144
00:10:58,740 --> 00:11:01,890
- Don't be shy.
- You two are the perfect pair!

145
00:11:01,890 --> 00:11:05,430
- Stop that, seriously.
- Aw, you'll break his heart.

146
00:11:29,910 --> 00:11:32,620
Apologize first.

147
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:36,060
Then, get my notebook back.

148
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:38,660
All right, you can do this.

149
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:40,390
You can do this.

150
00:11:40,390 --> 00:11:42,270
You can do this.

151
00:11:47,690 --> 00:11:49,580
Okay.

152
00:11:51,770 --> 00:11:53,230
Damn...

153
00:11:53,230 --> 00:11:55,600
- One more round!
- You're on.

154
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:57,200
There!

155
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,410
Go, go!

156
00:11:58,410 --> 00:12:01,160
<i>I can't do this! I can't!</i>

157
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:03,730
<i>It's impossible!</i>

158
00:12:08,570 --> 00:12:11,710
Lunch showdown in three,

159
00:12:11,710 --> 00:12:14,080
two, one...

160
00:12:16,230 --> 00:12:17,350
That's a strong contender.

161
00:12:17,350 --> 00:12:20,010
<i>Those four practically sparkle.</i>

162
00:12:20,010 --> 00:12:23,230
<i>I could never call out to them.</i>

163
00:12:23,230 --> 00:12:25,810
Store-bought isn't homemade. Disqualified.

164
00:12:25,810 --> 00:12:27,020
It's made somewhere!

165
00:12:27,020 --> 00:12:28,360
It's not the same.

166
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:30,840
See? Look at my beautiful lunch.

167
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,720
Not bad.

168
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:35,180
It's cute.

169
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:39,110
All right, let's start with warm-ups.

170
00:12:39,110 --> 00:12:41,590
Find a partner and get stretching.

171
00:12:41,590 --> 00:12:43,710
Whoever's left, come to me.

172
00:12:43,710 --> 00:12:46,090
- You ready?
- Yeah.

173
00:12:46,090 --> 00:12:49,160
Sit down.

174
00:12:49,160 --> 00:12:51,640
Come on, Serizawa.

175
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:53,440
Sorry, not today.

176
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:55,280
Suzuki.

177
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:58,620
Let's get stretching.

178
00:12:58,620 --> 00:13:01,300
- Huh?
- Are even you trying?

179
00:13:01,300 --> 00:13:02,790
You're as stiff as a board.

180
00:13:02,790 --> 00:13:05,120
- You can go farther.
- Ow!

181
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:08,130
Breath out, and hold.

182
00:13:08,130 --> 00:13:10,710
<i>I don't understand.</i>

183
00:13:10,710 --> 00:13:13,320
<i>Why is Serizawa stretching with me?</i>

184
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:19,630
<i>He has to be mad about yesterday...</i>

185
00:13:19,630 --> 00:13:23,800
Takeuchi? Why're you paired with Usami?

186
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:26,740
Serizawa dumped me.

187
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:29,260
Aw...

188
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:30,960
Poor you!

189
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:34,070
Hey! It's not so bad working out with me.

190
00:13:34,070 --> 00:13:35,250
Whatever you say.

191
00:13:35,250 --> 00:13:37,410
Right, Takeuchi?

192
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:41,410
I guess.

193
00:13:41,410 --> 00:13:43,590
See?

194
00:13:43,590 --> 00:13:48,010
Has Serizawa even spoken to Suzuki before?

195
00:13:52,710 --> 00:13:55,120
Focus on your own stretches.

196
00:13:57,050 --> 00:14:02,330
<i>I feel like everyone's staring at us.</i>

197
00:14:02,330 --> 00:14:04,850
<i>And is it just me, or...</i>

198
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:10,090
<i>Is he really close?</i>

199
00:14:12,270 --> 00:14:15,660
You okay?

200
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:17,430
Are you feeling sick?

201
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:25,070
I'm fine.

202
00:14:26,010 --> 00:14:29,860
But your ears.

203
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:31,680
They're turning red.

204
00:14:38,220 --> 00:14:41,890
<i>Get me out of here!</i>

205
00:14:41,890 --> 00:14:46,350
Mr. Usami, can I take Suzuki to the nurse?
He's looking sick.

206
00:14:46,350 --> 00:14:48,380
Huh?

207
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:50,410
Sure. Take it easy, Suzuki.

208
00:14:50,410 --> 00:14:52,310
N-No, I'm...

209
00:14:52,310 --> 00:14:54,910
Here, hop on.

210
00:14:54,910 --> 00:14:56,220
But...

211
00:14:56,220 --> 00:14:58,070
Don't keep me hanging.

212
00:15:09,930 --> 00:15:13,450
Serizawa...

213
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:16,960
Sorry.

214
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:21,820
- I'm not actually sick.
- Yeah.

215
00:15:21,820 --> 00:15:23,620
I know.

216
00:15:23,620 --> 00:15:25,070
Huh?

217
00:15:25,850 --> 00:15:29,430
Then where are we going?

218
00:15:30,770 --> 00:15:33,400
Somewhere we can be alone.

219
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:44,230
The classroom?

220
00:15:47,910 --> 00:15:50,960
Your stop, sir.

221
00:15:50,960 --> 00:15:52,860
Thanks.

222
00:15:53,890 --> 00:15:58,160
I could tell you wanted to talk.

223
00:15:58,160 --> 00:16:01,650
So, I figured it'd be easier if we were alone.

224
00:16:01,650 --> 00:16:03,030
Here.

225
00:16:06,150 --> 00:16:08,880
T-Thanks.

226
00:16:10,140 --> 00:16:12,320
So...
[Idea Journal]

227
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:17,670
About this notebook...

228
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:40,910
Do you write BL?

229
00:16:43,650 --> 00:16:46,940
Yeah.

230
00:16:48,090 --> 00:16:51,470
Since you're basing a character off me,

231
00:16:51,470 --> 00:16:54,650
does that mean...

232
00:16:54,650 --> 00:16:56,780
You like me, Suzuki?

233
00:17:03,870 --> 00:17:07,320
Hey, don't shy away.

234
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:13,000
Give me an answer.

235
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:18,750
I, uh...

236
00:17:21,190 --> 00:17:22,860
I...

237
00:17:25,180 --> 00:17:26,540
I'm so sorry!

238
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:29,740
Huh? Wait, I'm confused.

239
00:17:29,740 --> 00:17:33,040
I used your likeness without your permission,

240
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:35,340
and caused a major misunderstanding.

241
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:38,050
I'm so terribly sorry!

242
00:17:38,050 --> 00:17:39,450
Suzuki, look at me.

243
00:17:39,450 --> 00:17:41,380
I just enjoy BL works.

244
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:46,450
I even think you're the ideal top.

245
00:17:46,450 --> 00:17:51,090
But my romantic orientation

246
00:17:51,090 --> 00:17:53,390
has nothing to do with my BL hobby.

247
00:17:53,390 --> 00:17:58,080
So, I never looked at you in that way.

248
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:02,020
I see.

249
00:18:02,020 --> 00:18:05,470
I'm sorry I made you feel uncomfortable.

250
00:18:05,470 --> 00:18:08,150
I'll try to make it up to you.

251
00:18:09,430 --> 00:18:11,810
How?

252
00:18:11,810 --> 00:18:13,940
I can pay for the damage done?

253
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:17,640
Actually, I'm too broke for that...

254
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:21,870
But I promise I'll do whatever I can.

255
00:18:21,870 --> 00:18:23,760
Really? Anything?

256
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:25,420
Yeah.

257
00:18:26,430 --> 00:18:28,480
So...

258
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:30,460
I mean...

259
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:37,850
Please don't tell anyone else about this.

260
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:47,770
All right, deal.

261
00:18:47,770 --> 00:18:50,190
Then how's this?

262
00:18:58,650 --> 00:19:00,310
Let me read it.

263
00:19:00,310 --> 00:19:02,580
That novel of yours.

264
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:04,040
Huh?

265
00:19:04,040 --> 00:19:06,460
I should clear something up.

266
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:08,270
I'm not mad at you.

267
00:19:08,270 --> 00:19:11,190
If anything, I'm honored.

268
00:19:12,180 --> 00:19:13,770
Huh?

269
00:19:13,770 --> 00:19:16,230
I also think I'm a top.

270
00:19:16,230 --> 00:19:17,860
What?

271
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:19,550
Right, sorry.

272
00:19:19,550 --> 00:19:22,110
I'm actually a BL fan, too.

273
00:19:22,940 --> 00:19:24,270
You are?

274
00:19:24,270 --> 00:19:26,440
Is it that surprising?

275
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:29,200
Yeah.

276
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:32,880
Why? Anyone can read BL, right?

277
00:19:35,510 --> 00:19:38,130
So, what sort of stuff do you read?

278
00:19:38,130 --> 00:19:42,190
I like Tatakiwari Ishibashi's works.

279
00:19:42,190 --> 00:19:44,640
I like their works, too.

280
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:47,330
Seriously? A fellow fan with great taste!

281
00:19:47,330 --> 00:19:49,260
Give me five!

282
00:19:51,170 --> 00:19:53,110
Five.

283
00:19:56,400 --> 00:20:00,940
Now I really want to read your novel.

284
00:20:02,670 --> 00:20:05,260
Well...

285
00:20:05,260 --> 00:20:06,750
You said you'd do anything.

286
00:20:06,750 --> 00:20:09,310
But my writing isn't good.

287
00:20:09,310 --> 00:20:12,170
And it's not done.

288
00:20:12,170 --> 00:20:16,980
Not to mention no one else
has read it before...

289
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:21,020
Then I guess I get to be your very first.

290
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:22,040
Huh?

291
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:24,370
Come on, please?

292
00:20:24,370 --> 00:20:26,160
Give me the honor

293
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:29,900
of being your first reader.

294
00:20:34,740 --> 00:20:37,430
That's a good line.

295
00:20:37,430 --> 00:20:40,040
Oh, did that one get to you?

296
00:20:40,790 --> 00:20:42,220
Yeah.

297
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:49,740
But how about this instead?

298
00:20:51,310 --> 00:20:56,120
"Suzuki, give me all your very firsts".

299
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:58,610
That's a good one!

300
00:20:58,610 --> 00:21:00,400
Let me give it another go.

301
00:21:05,010 --> 00:21:06,980
Suzuki.

302
00:21:06,980 --> 00:21:10,750
Give me all your very firsts.

303
00:21:16,010 --> 00:21:17,530
How was that?

304
00:21:23,510 --> 00:21:25,190
Suzuki?

305
00:21:26,610 --> 00:21:28,640
Hello?

306
00:21:30,030 --> 00:21:31,730
You okay?

307
00:21:33,310 --> 00:21:35,640
That...

308
00:21:35,640 --> 00:21:37,180
Was...

309
00:21:38,820 --> 00:21:41,810
Amazing.

310
00:21:41,810 --> 00:21:44,020
You scared me for a second there.

311
00:21:44,020 --> 00:21:46,330
So, how about it?

312
00:21:46,330 --> 00:21:49,980
Will you give me the honor
of being your first?

313
00:21:49,980 --> 00:21:51,680
Yes, or no?

314
00:21:53,290 --> 00:21:57,380
If you want it, it's all yours.

315
00:21:59,070 --> 00:22:00,780
I'll take it.

316
00:22:10,300 --> 00:22:12,640
You froze up again.

317
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:17,540
Can you blame me? That was a dirty move.

318
00:22:17,540 --> 00:22:19,460
Aw, cute.

319
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:25,420
<i>This was how Serizawa began reading my novel.</i>

320
00:22:25,420 --> 00:22:29,370
Let's meet on the roof tomorrow for lunch.

321
00:22:29,370 --> 00:22:31,150
Sure.

322
00:22:31,970 --> 00:22:37,070
<i>But what I didn't realize at the time...</i>

323
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:42,250
<i>Was that the popular Serizawa</i>

324
00:22:42,250 --> 00:22:47,770
<i>acts weird around me!</i>

325
00:22:47,770 --> 00:22:49,860
Suzuki. Suzuki? Suzuki!

326
00:22:49,860 --> 00:22:52,170
You'll be eating lunch with me from now on.

327
00:22:52,170 --> 00:22:54,320
- Huh?
- We're learning to be friends!

328
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:56,910
Most tops are great cooks.

329
00:22:56,910 --> 00:22:58,110
- Really?
- Leave this to me.

330
00:22:58,110 --> 00:23:00,210
I'm going to be the King of Stewing!

331
00:23:00,210 --> 00:23:02,140
I just don't know...

